  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Welcome to episode five of Kukhnya season five. Max Lavrov rushes back to Moscow after learning that Vika is pregnant, but when he catches up to her at the hotel, she hits him with a shocking claim.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Минуту ничего не пить!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Огузок вернулся!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вика, подожди!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нам нужно поговорить!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я знаю, что ты беременная!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Кто тебе сказал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не важно, кто мне это сказал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Главное, что я здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я готов быть отцом этого ребёнка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Как благородно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Расслабься.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Это не твой ребёнок.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Минуту ничего не пить!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do not drink anything for a minute!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'a minute' and finishing on 'drink'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Огузок вернулся!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The rookie has returned!' The '-l' ending on the verb meaning 'returned' places the action in the masculine past tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вика, подожди!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vika, wait!' An emphatic spoken line centered on the verb meaning 'wait'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нам нужно поговорить!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We need to talk!' Max brings out the contrast between 'us' and 'needed' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я знаю, что ты беременная!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I know that you are pregnant!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'I' and finishing on 'pregnant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Кто тебе сказал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who told you?' The grammar packs 'who' and 'said' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не важно, кто мне это сказал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It does not matter who told me this.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'not' and finishing on 'said'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Главное, что я здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The main thing is that I am here.' Max brings out the contrast between 'the main thing' and 'what' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я готов быть отцом этого ребёнка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am ready to be the father of this child.' Max anchors the line on 'I', while 'child' completes the thought. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Как благородно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How noble.' The grammar packs 'how' and 'noble' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Расслабься.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Relax.' The meaning hinges on 'relax' working together with 'relax' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Это не твой ребёнок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is not your child.' Vika addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'child'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
